  "content": {
    "id": "p39-q20-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "Athletes' finishing times varied between 3 and 7 minutes, represented by the continuous PDF $f(x)=\\frac{1}{116}(x^3-9x^2+24x+1)$ on $[3,7]$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p39-q20-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the CDF.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$F(x)=\\begin{cases}0,&x<3,\\\\\\dfrac{x^4-12x^3+48x^2+4x-201}{464},&3\\le x\\le7,\\\\1,&x>7.\\end{cases}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}F(x)&=\\int_3^x\\frac{1}{116}(t^3-9t^2+24t+1)\\,dt\\\\&=\\frac{1}{116}\\left[\\frac{t^4}{4}-3t^3+12t^2+t\\right]_3^x\\\\&=\\frac{x^4-12x^3+48x^2+4x-201}{464},\\qquad 3\\le x\\le7.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $F(x)=0$ for $x<3$ and $F(x)=1$ for $x>7$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q20-b",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the probability that an athlete finishes:",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p39-q20-b-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "in less than 5 minutes",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{9}{29}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(X<5)&=F(5)\\\\&=\\frac{625-1500+1200+20-201}{464}\\\\&=\\frac{144}{464}\\\\&=\\frac{9}{29}.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 23
          },
          {
            "id": "p39-q20-b-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "in 4 minutes or more",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{393}{464}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(X\\ge4)&=1-F(4)\\\\&=1-\\frac{256-768+768+16-201}{464}\\\\&=1-\\frac{71}{464}\\\\&=\\frac{393}{464}.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 23
          },
          {
            "id": "p39-q20-b-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "in between 4 and 5 minutes",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{73}{464}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(4\\le X\\le5)&=F(5)-F(4)\\\\&=\\frac{144}{464}-\\frac{71}{464}\\\\&=\\frac{73}{464}.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 19
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q20-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What is the most likely finishing time?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "7 minutes.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\frac{1}{116}(3x^2-18x+24).\\end{align*}$$\n$f'(x)=0\\;\\rightarrow\\;x^2-6x+8=0\\;\\rightarrow\\;x=2\\text{ or }x=4$.\nOnly $x=4$ is in $[3,7]$.\nCheck the endpoints and stationary point:\n$$f(3)=\\frac{19}{116},\\qquad f(4)=\\frac{17}{116},\\qquad f(7)=\\frac{71}{116}.$$\nThe maximum density occurs at $x=7$, so the mode is 7 minutes.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      }
    ]
  },
